# Options Chain Download

Downloads 1-minute aggregate bars for individual option contracts via the Massive REST API, with split-adjusted prices (`adjusted=True`). Designed to capture a tradable subset of the options chain (ATM ±10-20% moneyness) rather than every listed contract.

## Scripts

| Script | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `options_chain_discover.py` | Queries `list_options_contracts` to build a contract manifest CSV |
| `options_chain_download.py` | Downloads 1-min aggregates per contract, merges with underlying OHLCV |
| `options_chain_parallel_download.py` | Parallel dispatcher — spawns workers, tracks state, resume support |
| `options_chain_parallel_status.py` | Status monitor — `--watch` / `--kill` support |

## Workflow

```bash
# 1. Discover contracts (one API call per ticker, paginated)
python scripts/options/options_chain_discover.py --ohlcv_tickers --year 2025
python scripts/options/options_chain_discover.py --tickers AAPL,TSLA --year 2025
python scripts/options/options_chain_discover.py --tickers_file data/universes/2025/combined_unique.csv --year 2025

# 2. Download chains (parallel, ~2-3 API calls per contract)
python scripts/options/options_chain_parallel_download.py --ohlcv_tickers --year 2025 --spawn 50
python scripts/options/options_chain_parallel_download.py --tickers AAPL --year 2025 --spawn 16
python scripts/options/options_chain_parallel_download.py --tickers AAPL --year 2025 --aggregate 1sec --spawn 16
python scripts/options/options_chain_parallel_download.py --tickers_file /tmp/missing.txt --year 2025 --spawn 50 --resume

# 3. Monitor
python scripts/options/options_chain_parallel_status.py --year 2025 --watch
python scripts/options/options_chain_parallel_status.py --year 2025 --aggregate 1sec --watch

# 4. Kill if needed
python scripts/options/options_chain_parallel_status.py --year 2025 --kill

# 5. Resume from interrupted run
rm data/options/chains/.parallel_state_2025_1min_chains.json
python scripts/options/options_chain_parallel_download.py --ohlcv_tickers --year 2025 --spawn 50 --resume
```

## Arguments (parallel dispatcher)

| Argument | Required | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `--tickers` | No* | — | Comma-separated ticker symbols |
| `--tickers_file` | No* | — | Path to CSV with `ticker` column |
| `--ohlcv_tickers` | No* | — | Derive tickers from `data/SPY/1min/<year>/` |
| `--year` | Yes | — | Year, e.g. `2025` |
| `--aggregate` | No | `1min` | `1min` or `1sec` |
| `--spawn` | Yes | — | Number of parallel worker processes |
| `--resume` | No | off | Skip tickers with existing output files |
| `--output` | No | `data/` | Base output directory |
| `--check` | No | — | Skip tickers with files in `<dir>/options/chains/<agg>/<year>/` |
| `--delay` | No | `0.1` | Sleep seconds between API calls in workers |
| `--logs` | No | off | Save dispatcher log file |
| `--manifest` | No | `data/options/chains/contract_manifest_<year>.csv` | Custom manifest path |

*One of `--tickers`, `--tickers_file`, or `--ohlcv_tickers` is required.

## Arguments (discovery)

| Argument | Required | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `--moneyness_pct` | No | `0.20` | Max absolute moneyness as fraction (±20%) |
| `--delay` | No | `0.25` | Sleep seconds between API calls |

## Output layout

```
data/options/chains/
├── contract_manifest_<year>.csv    ← Contract discovery output
├── .parallel_state_<year>_<agg>_chains.json  ← Dispatcher state
├── parallel_report_<year>_<agg>_chains.json  ← Run report
├── logs/                           ← Log files
├── 1min/
│   └── <year>/
│       ├── <ticker>_<year>_1min_chains.csv  ← Final output
│       ├── processing/             ← Staging (in-progress files)
│       ├── no_data/                ← Header-only files (no data)
│       └── errors/                 ← Failed downloads
└── 1sec/
    └── <year>/
        ├── <ticker>_<year>_1sec_chains.csv
        └── ...
```

With `--output <dir>`:
```
<dir>/options/chains/<agg>/<year>/<ticker>_<year>_<agg>_chains.csv
```

## Output columns (31)

```
ticker, timestamp, contract_symbol, strike, call_put, expiry, days_to_expiry,
expiry_type, open, high, low, close, volume, vwap, transactions,
underlying_price, moneyness,
intrinsic_value, extrinsic_value, mid,
bid, ask, spread, implied_volatility, delta, gamma, theta, vega
```

- **Fully populated**: `ticker` through `transactions` (from aggs), `expiry_type` (computed), `underlying_price` through `moneyness` (from OHLCV join + computed), `intrinsic_value`, `extrinsic_value`, `mid` (computed)
- **Forward-filled**: `close` and `underlying_price` carry forward the last known value when an API bar has no trade or when timestamp alignment misses the stock minute
- **Computed fields**:
  - `intrinsic_value` = max(underlying - strike, 0) for calls; max(strike - underlying, 0) for puts
  - `extrinsic_value` = close - intrinsic_value
  - `mid` = close (as best available; bid/ask reserved for future quotes join)
  - `expiry_type` = Monthly (3rd Friday), Weekly (other Fridays or DTE ≤ 7), sorted by convention
  - `moneyness` = (strike - underlying_price) / underlying_price
- **Placeholder (empty)**: `bid`, `ask`, `spread`, `implied_volatility`, `delta`, `gamma`, `theta`, `vega` — computed later

## Contract filtering (discovery)

Contracts are filtered by:
1. **Expiration range**: `year-01-01` to `(year+1)-03-31`
2. **Moneyness**: `|strike - mid_price| / mid_price ≤ moneyness_pct` (default ±20%)
3. **Underlying price range**: derived from `data/SPY/1min/<year>/` (or `data/SPY/1D/` fallback)

## Staging and finalization

- Workers write to `processing/<ticker>_<year>_chains.csv`
- On success, the dispatcher renames `processing/` → final immediately (per-ticker, no batch finalization)
- Files with only a header row go to `no_data/`
- Failed downloads (exceptions) go to `errors/`
- `--resume` checks the final directory only (not `processing/`)

## API details

- **`list_options_contracts`**: Paginated, `expired=True` for historical contracts, up to 1000 per page
- **`list_aggs`**: `adjusted=True`, 50K bars per call limit, ~2-3 calls per contract per year
- Each ticker typically has 2,000-5,000 contracts within 20% moneyness, most with negligible volume
- API call count scales with contract count, not trading activity — use `--spawn` conservatively

## Notes

- `adjusted=True` is applied server-side — all prices are split-adjusted
- Underlying OHLCV reads from `data/SPY/1min/<year>/` (.csv or .csv.gz)
- Contract symbols use standard OCC format: `O:<TICKER><YYMMDD><C|P><strike*1000>`
- IV and Greeks placeholders are left empty — compute locally with your preferred pricing library
- `close` and `underlying_price` are forward-filled per contract: if a minute bar has no trade, or the underlying OHLCV has no matching timestamp, the last known value carries forward
- `mid` currently holds the `close` price; when bid/ask data becomes available (quotes_v1 S3 flat files or snapshots), `mid = (bid + ask) / 2`
- `expiry_type` classification: 3rd Friday → Monthly, other Friday or DTE ≤ 7 → Weekly
